<problem>

<setup>
  <select name="a">
    <option selectWeight="2">
      <selectFromSequence from="-10" to="10" exclude="0" excludecombinations="(1 -1) (-1 1)" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="false" />
    </option>
    <option>
      <group>
        $temp $temp
      </group>
      <selectFromSequence from="-10" to="10" exclude="-1 0 1" name="temp" />
    </option>
  </select>

  <select name="x">x y z</select>

  <math name="factored_quadratic" simplify="full">($x+$a[1][1][1])($x+$a[1][1][2])</math>
  <math name="expanded_quadratic" simplify="full" expand="true"><math extend="$factored_quadratic" /></math>
  <convertSetToList name="zero_list" simplify="full"><math>{-$a[1][1][1],-$a[1][1][2]}</math></convertSetToList>
  <math name="factor1" simplify="full">$x+$a[1][1][1]</math>
  <math name="factor2" simplify="full">$x+$a[1][1][2]</math>
  <math name="minus_a" simplify="full">-$a[1][1][1]</math>
  <math name="minus_b" simplify="full">-$a[1][1][2]</math>

</setup>

Solve the equation <m><math extend="$expanded_quadratic" /> =0</m>.

<p>How many solutions are there? <mathInput name="user_num_sol" /></p>

<p>The solutions are:</p>

<repeatForSequence length="min(10,$user_num_sol)" name="xs">
    <p><m>x =</m> <mathInput /></p>
  </repeatForSequence>

<answer>
  <award>
    <when matchpartial="true">
      <mathList>
        <setup><collect componentType="mathInput" from="$xs" isResponse="true" name="collect_list" /></setup><mathList name="list" extend="$collect_list.value" />
      </mathList>
      =
      <convertSetToList extend="$zero_list" />
    </when>
  </award>

</answer>



<solution>
Factoring the quadratic <m><math extend="$expanded_quadratic" /></m>, we obtain <m><math extend="$factored_quadratic" /></m>.  Therefore, the solutions to 
<me><math extend="$expanded_quadratic" /> =0</me>
are the same as the solutions to
<me><math extend="$factored_quadratic" />=0.</me>

<conditionalContent>
  <case condition="$a[1][1][1]=$a[1][1][2]">
  The equation reduces to <m><math extend="$factor1" />=0</m> so that the only solution is <m>$x = <math extend="$minus_a" /></m>.
  </case>
  <else>
  For this factored expression to be zero, one of the factors must be zero.  Either <m><math extend="$factor1" />=0</m> or <m><math extend="$factor2" />=0</m>.  Therefore, there are two solutions <m>$x=<math extend="$minus_a" /></m> and <m>$x=<math extend="$minus_b" /></m>.
  </else>
</conditionalContent>

</solution>

</problem>